      "writtenOn": "2023-01-05T18:23:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As a concrete example, for this vendor module\n```\nandroid_app {\n  name: \"foo\",\n  vendor: true,\n  sdk_version: \"current\",\n  min_sdk_version: \"25\",\n}\n\n# Product config\nBOARD_CURRENT_API_LEVEL_FOR_VENDOR_MODULES :\u003d 29\n```\n\nJeongik, what value should be passed to `--min-sdk-version` and `--target-sdk-version` for aapt2? \n\nOn ToT, it is 25. Should it be BOARD_CURRENT_API_LEVEL_FOR_VENDOR_MODULES instead? (29 in this example, or 28, or 27, ...)\n\n(I am refactoring min_sdk_version, and would not like to cause a regression in functionality)",
